    <description>Fires when AF_DiscountApprovalStatus__c changes to Approved. 2026-09-10 fix: the approval chain previously only sent notifications and never actually applied the approved discount to price - Quote.AF_DiscountAmount__c/AF_DiscountPercent__c drove tier routing but nothing wrote it onto any QuoteLineItem, so TotalPrice never changed even after Approved (meanwhile QuoteLineItem&apos;s own native Discount/DiscountAmount fields and the separately-named QuoteLineItem.AF_DiscountAmount__c/AF_DiscountPercentage__c custom fields were directly editable and bypassed approval entirely, since nothing gated them - QuoteLineItem-level discount editing has since been removed from the layout and FLS to close that gap, see AF_PS_QuoteLineItem_FullAccess). Notifies the Quote Owner via email and Custom Notification - same dual-channel pattern as AF_FL_Reservation_Approved. logEmailOnSend+relatedRecordId=$Record.Id added so the email logs as an EmailMessage on the Quote&apos;s own Emails/Activity related list (previously sent but not logged anywhere). 2026-09-09: upgraded from plain text to branded HTML (sendRichBody=true). Tried real EmailTemplate + AF_SendTemplateEmailAction (Apex wrapper around Messaging.sendEmail(templateId=...)) first, since Flow&apos;s own &quot;emailTemplate&quot; core action is confirmed NOT a valid InvocableActionType in this org&apos;s Metadata API - but Messaging.sendEmail to a User target hard-requires saveAsActivity=false, and with that forced false, ZERO EmailMessage row is created (confirmed empirically: isSuccess()=true, no EmailMessage ever appears), unlike emailSimple+logEmailOnSend which reliably logs even to User recipients. Reverted to emailSimple/inline-HTML for this reason - it is the only mechanism proven to both send AND log for a User recipient in this org.

2026-09-14 change: the approved discount % used to be written to only the single Vehicle line item (AF_LineItemType__c=Vehicle), leaving every other line (add-ons/accessories) undiscounted. Live business feedback: the approved discount should apply to the whole Quote, i.e. every QuoteLineItem, not just the vehicle. Replaced the single Get_Vehicle_Line/Apply_Discount_To_Line pair with Get_All_Lines feeding Loop_All_Lines, which sets each line&apos;s native Discount (Percent) field to Quote.AF_DiscountPercent__c and collects them into var_LinesToUpdate for one bulk Update_All_Lines DML after the loop - Salesforce recalculates each line&apos;s TotalPrice, and Quote.TotalPrice/Subtotal/GrandTotal, from that automatically. Get_All_Lines excludes AF_LineItemType__c = &quot;Trade-In Deduction&quot; and &quot;Discount Adjustment&quot;: these aren&apos;t priced items, they&apos;re already-negative adjustment lines, and live-testing found touching a Trade-In Deduction line re-triggers AF_VR_QLI_TradeInDeductionGate (its own unrelated validation requiring an Approved+Accepted linked Trade-In), which can fail the whole Approved transaction for a reason that has nothing to do with the discount. If the Quote has no discountable lines, the update collection stays empty and Update_All_Lines silently no-ops.

LFRDN-755 (2026-09-27): this flow applied Quote.AF_DiscountPercent__c to every line, but that field is a
native Salesforce formula (IF(Subtotal=0,0,AF_DiscountAmount__c/Subtotal)) that always divides by the
FULL Subtotal, including the negative Trade-In Deduction line - fixing the tier-routing calculation
in AF_FL_Quote_SetDiscountApprovalStatus alone (also done as part of this ticket) does NOT fix this
flow, since AF_DiscountPercent__c is a separate, independently-computed field this flow reads
directly - confirmed live: after fixing tier routing only, this flow still applied the old wrong 6.08%
instead of the correct ~4.02% (16,000 approved on a 398,300 gross with a 135,000 trade-in). Added a
first pass (Loop_Sum_Lines/AF_Formula_SumLineGross) over the exact same Get_All_Lines collection this
flow already excludes Trade-In Deduction/Discount Adjustment from, summing UnitPrice*Quantity (not
TotalPrice, which would already have a prior Discount% baked in and corrupt the calculation on a
second approval cycle) into var_DiscountableGrossTotal; the second pass then applies
AF_Formula_CorrectedDiscountPercent (AF_DiscountAmount__c / that gross total) instead of the native
field. The two loops iterate the same already-queried Get_All_Lines collection, so no extra SOQL.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_CorrectedDiscountPercent</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!var_DiscountableGrossTotal} = 0, 0, ({!$Record.AF_DiscountAmount__c} / {!var_DiscountableGrossTotal}) * 100)</expression>
        <scale>4</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_Subject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Approved: Quote Discount &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_SumLineGross</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>{!Loop_Sum_Lines.UnitPrice} * {!Loop_Sum_Lines.Quantity}</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;margin:0;padding:16px;background-color:#F4F4F6;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #E2E5EA;border-top:4px solid #1E7A46;padding:20px 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;display:inline-block;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:3px;background-color:#DFF3E6;color:#1E7A46;font-size:11px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.5px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:12px;&quot;&gt;Approved&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;color:#0B2545;&quot;&gt;Quote Discount Approved&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;Your discount request on Quote &lt;strong&gt;&apos; &amp; {!$Record.Name} &amp; &apos;&lt;/strong&gt; has been approved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;You can proceed with the quotation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&apos;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Your discount request on Quote &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name} &amp; &quot; was approved.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifTitle</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Discount Approved: &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name}</expression>
    </formulas>
